<title>USA: Montana row crop harvest done, weather turns cold.</title>
<headline>Montana row crop harvest done, weather turns cold.</headline>
<dateline>HELENA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Extremely cold temperatures chilled Montana in the week ended Sunday but producers managed to finish row crop harvesting, the state's Agricultural Statistics Service said in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Winter wheat was 85 percent emerged, against the five-year average of 79 percent. The crop was rated four percent poor, 51 percent fair, 40 percent good and five percent excellent.</p>
<p>Sugar beets were 99 percent harvested, ahead of the five-year average of 95 percent.</p>
<p>Pasture and range were rated five percent very poor, 29 percent poor, 40 fair, 25 good and one percent excellent.</p>
<p>Topsoil moisture was rated 12 percent very short, 30 percent short, 51 percent adequate and seven percent surplus.</p>
<p>There were 3.7 days rated suitable for fieldwork.</p>
<p>---Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
